<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Wen of Liu Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">407–453</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Liu Yilong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Wen of Liu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, born Liu Yilong, was a son of the dynasty's founder Liu Yu and reigned from 424 to 453. His Yuanjia era brought prosperity and cultural achievement to the southern court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>, though his campaigns against the Northern Wei failed. He was murdered by his own heir, Liu Shao, in 453.</p></div>
